From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: win32u: a window is not shown black before its program paints it

David: windows flash black when they open. X exposes a window as soon as it
is shown, before the program has painted; win32u answered by sending the
whole surface, whose unpainted parts are zero -- black -- and later flushes
sent only what had been painted, over that black (QA VM, Notepad: the whole
window black for 40 ms, then its client area black for 35 ms more). Now a new
surface starts in the window colour (COLOR_WINDOW), as Windows shows an
unpainted window; its first flush sends all of it; and an exposed window is
sent again from its surface only once it has been drawn (its painting sends
it). struct window_surface gains a "drawn" flag.

Gate: make test-firstpaint (and on the QA VM, 230 fps captures of Notepad
opening: black frames in 3 of 3 runs before, 0 of 4 after).
